COMPLEX = [
("h2", "G. Computational Complexity"),
("p", "Let $c_{\\Phi}$ denote the cost of one encoder pass, $c_g$ the probe cost per raw frame, $d$ the transformer width and $L$ its depth. With $M=1+2K+B$ tokens, the cost per video is"),
("eq", "\\mathcal{C}(K,B)=R\\,c_{g}+K\\,c_{\\Phi}+L\\left(12Md^{2}+2M^{2}d\\right)", "cost"),
("p", "The three terms correspond to the probe, the encoder and the temporal model. Dense joint attention over $T$ frames would instead cost $T\\,c_{\\Phi}+L(12M_Td^2+2M_T^2d)$ with $M_T=1+T(1+N)$. The probe term is linear in $R$ with a very small constant, the encoder term is linear in $K$ instead of $T$, and the quadratic term depends on $B$ instead of $KN$. Memory follows the same pattern: the temporal model stores $O(LM^2)$ attention entries. Sorting for the quantile search costs $O(T)$ per video because $F$ is monotone, and top-$B$ selection costs $O(KN\\log B)$. Training cost is dominated by the encoder calls when features are not cached; in the experiments the encoder outputs of all lattice frames are cached once, which changes wall-clock time but not the per-video costs that the method would incur online."),
]
